255
01:17:37,659 --> 01:17:41,500
So we have to see in detail what is summarizing.

256
01:17:42,180 --> 01:17:48,279
A summary is a short retelling of a longer written passage containing the author's most important ideas.

257
01:17:49,140 --> 01:17:52,500
Summarizing helps improve both your reading and writing skills,

258
01:17:52,500 --> 01:17:58,560
and to summarize you must read a passage closely, finding the main ideas and supporting ideas.

259
01:17:58,980 --> 01:18:01,560
This section is very important, okay, about it.

260
01:18:02,800 --> 01:18:07,800
It gives the details of the needed essential parts for summarizing.

261
01:18:08,460 --> 01:18:13,680
You need to find the main idea in the given text and the supporting ideas.

262
01:18:14,880 --> 01:18:19,340
Then you must briefly write down those ideas in a few sentences or paragraph.

263
01:18:19,340 --> 01:18:35,760
A few sentences is another key for us here because the summarized paragraph, summarized one, should be shorter than the original text, of course.

264
01:18:36,440 --> 01:18:39,899
The ideal form of it is nearly the half of it, right?

265
01:18:39,899 --> 01:18:44,640
Summaries have many uses in academic writing, like paraphrases.

266
01:18:44,819 --> 01:18:46,619
They can be used to support a point.

267
01:18:46,800 --> 01:18:52,539
They can also be part of a longer piece of writing, such as a book and report.

268
01:18:53,079 --> 01:18:57,300
You might summarize a book before going on to write a response to it.

269
01:18:58,000 --> 01:19:03,279
And writing a summary can also be a good strategy for remembering things that you have read.

270
01:19:03,279 --> 01:19:07,359
For example, your teacher may ask you to summarize a textbook chapter.

271
01:19:07,940 --> 01:19:10,359
We can use summarizing everywhere.

272
01:19:10,640 --> 01:19:12,100
It's very practical, okay?

273
01:19:12,420 --> 01:19:15,560
Because you don't need to cover the whole passage or the article.

274
01:19:16,180 --> 01:19:19,000
Just by looking at the summarized version of it,

275
01:19:19,420 --> 01:19:24,279
you can get the main ideas and the critical points about the issue there.

276
01:19:24,380 --> 01:19:25,699
So it is important.

277
01:19:25,699 --> 01:19:35,539
How is summary different from paraphrases?

278
01:19:36,079 --> 01:19:38,539
It's important to understand the difference.

279
01:19:40,239 --> 01:19:43,440
A paraphrase is simply rewriting passage.

280
01:19:43,640 --> 01:19:50,220
If you are asked to paraphrase the given paragraph or the given article,

281
01:19:50,220 --> 01:19:54,960
normally you are not given a whole article to paraphrase, just a sum of it.

282
01:19:55,699 --> 01:20:03,140
You need to change each sentence there into a different form with the same meaning.

283
01:20:03,940 --> 01:20:07,800
The number of the sentences are nearly the same, but in paraphrasing.

284
01:20:08,279 --> 01:20:09,800
But when you are doing summary,

285
01:20:11,819 --> 01:20:19,060
in a summary paragraph, it shouldn't be in the same length with the original material,

286
01:20:19,340 --> 01:20:23,859
rather than it should be just given in very limited sentences,

287
01:20:23,859 --> 01:20:32,539
and the main focus should be included as the author's main idea and the supporting ideas,

288
01:20:32,539 --> 01:20:35,859
if it has in the original text, okay?

289
01:20:36,640 --> 01:20:41,060
So a summary, on the other hand, contains only the main idea and the supporting ideas,

290
01:20:41,220 --> 01:20:44,279
and a summary will be much shorter, as I said.

291
01:20:44,420 --> 01:20:46,319
It should be shorter, right?

292
01:20:46,319 --> 01:20:53,039
It cannot be in the same length with the given article, with the given paragraph there.

293
01:20:54,779 --> 01:20:57,760
Okay, so you see how to summarize a paragraph here.

294
01:20:57,760 --> 01:20:59,199
